{"tool_name":"ascat","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","debian","biotools","bioconda","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"bioconda":{"name":"ascat","version":"3.2.0","home":"https://www.crick.ac.uk/research/a-z-researchers/researchers-v-y/peter-van-loo/software","documentation":"https://github.com/VanLoo-lab/ascat/blob/v3.2.0/README.md","license":"GPL-3.0-or-later","summary":"ASCAT is a method to derive copy number profiles of tumour cells,\naccounting for normal cell admixture and tumour aneuploidy (Figure 1).\nASCAT infers tumour purity (the fraction of tumour cells) and ploidy (the\namount of DNA per tumour cell, expressed as multiples of haploid genomes)\nfrom SNP array or massively parallel sequencing data, and calculates\nwhole-genome allele-specific copy number profiles (the number of copies of\nboth parental alleles for all SNP loci across the genome).\n","identifiers":["biotools:ascat","doi:10.1073/pnas.1009843107"],"build":{"noarch":"generic","number":1,"rpaths":["lib/R/lib/","lib/"],"run_exports":[null]},"requirements":{"host":["r-base","r-rcolorbrewer","r-r.devices","r-r.utils","r-data.table","r-doparallel","r-foreach","bioconductor-genomicranges","bioconductor-iranges"],"run":["r-base","r-rcolorbrewer","r-r.devices","r-r.utils","r-data.table","r-doparallel","r-foreach","bioconductor-genomicranges","bioconductor-iranges"]},"source_url":"https://github.com/VanLoo-lab/ascat/archive/refs/tags/v3.2.0.tar.gz","test":{"commands":["$R -e \"library(ASCAT)\""]}},"biocontainers":{"name":"ascat","identifiers":["biotools:ascat","doi:10.1073/pnas.1009843107"],"license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"Tool for accurate dissection of genome-wide allele-specific copy number in tumors. it accounts for normal cell admixture and tumor aneuploidy in the analysis of snp array data from cancer samples. it allows analysis of illumina and affymetrix snp array data of tumor samples (with or without matching germline samples).","home_url":"https://github.com/Crick-CancerGenomics/ascat","keyw